The CapCoal Mining Complex contains a number of leases and mines shown in figure 2 on the 221st page of 2020 EPBC 2018/8171 Independent Compliance Audit - Grasstree Mine EPBC Audit 2018:8171, https://web.archive.org/web/20250327203347/https://australia.angloamerican.com/~/media/Files/A/Anglo-American-Group-v5/Australia/sustainability/environment/EPBC2018_8171_2020_Ind_Audit.pdf, and includes the following: 
ML1831 (German Creek), granted  July 1979, expiring July 2040;
ML1998 (German Creek East) , granted Nov 1986, expiring Nov 2037;
ML70047 (German Creek South), granted July 1993, expiring July 2040;
ML70311 (Oak Park), granted Sep 2003 , expiring Sep 2033;
ML70336 (Lake Lindsay), granted April 2006, expiring April 2036. 
Mining lease geometries were extracted from the Queensland Mining Leases dataset (https://web.archive.org/web/2/https://www.data.qld.gov.au/dataset/queensland-mining-and-exploration-tenure-series/resource/f87794b8-7b9a-4732-89bb-56ccb2228d27). 
The boundary includes these leases and has an area of 333 square kilometers.
